>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `looper_ss`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.looper_ss : string * (simpExtLib.simpset -> tactic) ->
  simpExtLib.ssfrag
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Creates an extension fragment containing one looper.

Adding `looper_ss (name, mk)` to a simpset has the same effect as
`simpExtLib.add_looper (name, mk)`. The fragment is unnamed.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.++ (simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss,
     simpExtLib.looper_ss ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC));
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.add_looper`](#simpExtLib.add_looper),
[`simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC`](#simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC).
